menu "Keg Scale Display"

config KEG_DISPLAY_SLEEP_SECONDS
    int "Timer wake interval (seconds)"
    range 30 3600
    default 180
    help
        Normal deep-sleep timer wake interval. The display wakes, reads its paired
        scale once, refreshes e-paper only if useful data changed, then sleeps again.

config KEG_DISPLAY_SCAN_SECONDS
    int "Initial pairing scan duration (seconds)"
    range 2 30
    default 6

config KEG_DISPLAY_AUTO_PAIR_SINGLE
    bool "Automatically pair when exactly one compatible scale is visible"
    default y
    help
        If more than one compatible scale is visible, firmware never guesses.

config KEG_DISPLAY_TOUCH_WAKE
    bool "Use native capacitive touch on GPIO12 as a deep-sleep wake source"
    default y
    help
        GPIO12 is touch channel 5 on the classic ESP32 used by the T5 V2.3.1.
        Touch wake replaces the temporary GPIO39 EXT0 button wake because ESP32
        does not allow touch wake and EXT0 wake at the same time.

config KEG_DISPLAY_TOUCH_THRESHOLD_PERCENT
    int "Touch sensitivity threshold below baseline (percent)"
    depends on KEG_DISPLAY_TOUCH_WAKE
    range 1 50
    default 8
    help
        ESP32 touch values decrease when touched. The wake threshold is calibrated
        before each deep sleep as this percentage below the untouched benchmark.
        Lower values are more sensitive; higher values require a stronger touch.

config KEG_DISPLAY_TOUCH_INITIAL_WAIT_SECONDS
    int "Touch wake initial pour wait (seconds)"
    depends on KEG_DISPLAY_TOUCH_WAKE
    range 1 30
    default 10
    help
        After a capacitive-touch wake, keep the existing e-paper image visible
        and wait this long before the first BLE read. This gives the user time
        to begin and mostly complete a pour.

config KEG_DISPLAY_TOUCH_MAX_WAIT_SECONDS
    int "Touch wake maximum observation window (seconds)"
    depends on KEG_DISPLAY_TOUCH_WAKE
    range 5 60
    default 30
    help
        Maximum total time after a touch wake to wait for a meaningful stable
        scale change before returning to deep sleep. Normal successful reads
        still refresh as soon as the settled change is available; the extra
        headroom is only used for slow settling or transient BLE retries.

config KEG_DISPLAY_TOUCH_RETRY_SECONDS
    int "Touch wake retry interval (seconds)"
    depends on KEG_DISPLAY_TOUCH_WAKE
    range 1 10
    default 2
    help
        If the first post-touch read is unchanged or settling, wait this long
        before checking the scale again.

endmenu
